  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Minburn Technology Group has $767M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 453 awards. Minburn Technology Group averaged $1.7M per award in the current fiscal year to date. Minburn Technology Group obligations are down 18.9% year over year. Minburn Technology Group received the largest share of FY2026 obligations from the General Services Administration at $261M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $143M and the Department of State at $140M. Minburn Technology Group derives most of its FY2026 business from two NAICS markets: Other Computer Related Services at $396M and Software Publishers at $352M. Minburn Technology Group also records smaller activity in Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $11.1M and Computer Terminal and Other Computer Peripheral Equipment Manufacturing at $8.1M. Minburn Technology Group totals for prior fiscal years include $559M in FY21, $494M in FY22, $796M in FY23, $927M in FY24, and $946M in FY25.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main agency customers for Minburn Technology Group in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the largest buyer at $261M. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of State follow at $143M and $140M respectively. The Department of the Treasury and the Department of Energy account for $78.1M and $55.6M respectively, with smaller obligations from NASA at $32.5M and the Department of Defense at $15.1M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services drive Minburn Technology Group’s FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the top market at $396M. Software Publishers is the second market at $352M. Minburn Technology Group also records obligations in Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $11.1M and Computer Terminal and Other Computer Peripheral Equipment Manufacturing at $8.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
